          "answer": "Low iron can lead to fatigue because iron is a crucial component of hemoglobin, which is the protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout the body. Without enough iron, the body cannot produce enough healthy red blood cells, leading to reduced oxygen transport to vital organs and tissues. This can cause feelings of tiredness and weakness.\n\nUnfortunately, I cannot provide more detailed information on the biochemical mechanisms involved or specific pathways affected by low iron levels. If you have further questions or need clarification, feel free to ask!\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
